@startuml
title Course Registration — Sequence Diagram

actor Student
boundary "Course Catalog UI" as UI
control "Registration Service" as RS
database "Enrollment Database" as DB

== Browse offerings ==

Student -> UI: Browse offerings for semester
UI -> RS: getOfferings(semester)
RS -> DB: findOfferings(semester)
DB --> RS: Offerings with available places
RS --> UI: Catalog data
UI --> Student: Display course details and availability

== Register for an offering ==

Student -> UI: Register for offering
UI -> RS: register(studentId, offeringId)
RS -> DB: Begin atomic registration transaction

note over RS, DB
Registration uses one transaction.
Concurrent requests for the same offering
must serialize the capacity decision
or use an equivalent atomic conditional update.
end note

RS -> DB: Check offering exists
alt Offering does not exist
    DB --> RS: Rejected: offering not found
    RS -> DB: Roll back transaction
    RS --> UI: Registration rejected
    UI --> Student: Explain rejection
else Offering exists
    RS -> DB: Check student authorization
    alt Student is not authorized
        DB --> RS: Rejected: unauthorized
        RS -> DB: Roll back transaction
        RS --> UI: Registration rejected
        UI --> Student: Explain rejection
    else Student is authorized
        RS -> DB: Check UNIQUE(studentId, offeringId)
        alt Student already enrolled
            DB --> RS: Rejected: already enrolled
            RS -> DB: Roll back transaction
            RS --> UI: Registration rejected
            UI --> Student: "Already enrolled"
        else Student is not enrolled
            RS -> DB: Atomically reserve a place\nif enrolledCount < capacity
            alt No place remains
                DB --> RS: Rejected: course full
                RS -> DB: Roll back transaction
                RS --> UI: Registration rejected
                UI --> Student: "Course full"
            else Place reserved
                RS -> DB: Create Enrollment record
                RS -> DB: Increment enrolledCount
                note over DB
                Enrollment creation and count update
                commit together in one transaction.

                Invariant:
                enrolledCount equals the number
                of Enrollment records for the offering.

                If any operation fails, roll back
                both changes.
                end note
                RS -> DB: Commit transaction
                DB --> RS: Registration confirmed
                RS --> UI: Confirmation
                UI --> Student: Display confirmation
            end
        end
    end
end

@enduml
